    record={"keeps": "the authorship of the electronic-literature authors and artists whose works and materials are donated or collected, by author collection, journal or anthology",
            "name": "under the name the author published under, with a pen name kept as such: Wikipedia (third party) says the Marjorie C. Luesebrink Collection holds 66 works, 27 of them created and published under the pen name M.D. Coverley, and describes her as an artist 'who publishes under the name M. D. Coverley'; the ELO Repository page gives her as 'Marjorie C. Luesebrink (M.D. Coverley)'; the ELO Works collection page names a work under the pen name ('M. D. Coverley’s Egypt: The Book of Going Forth by Day') and lists works by creator under the author's name (a restored work, 'Amnesia: Restored (v2.5)', under 'Disch, Thomas M.'); a collaboratively designed work stands under its collective's name (Decameron Collective); how ELMS records an author name or pen name is not in the saved sources",
            "holder": "The NEXT, managed by the Electronic Literature Lab and supported by grants, donations and commissions; works 'owned or managed by the Electronic Literature Organization' (a project description, third party); author collections are donated by artists and scholars; access is open and online ('open-access, travel-free')",
            "function": "author collections hold an author's own works with donated materials, including personal copies of other authors' works; the museum re-creates, migrates and records video playthroughs of works made on obsolete software, and the work stays under its author; a collaborative work is held under its collective (nine Canadian artists and scholars for Decameron Collective); the saved sources show no attribution model for machine participation"},
