    ls_reading="The NEXT keeps electronic literature under the names its authors published under, and the saved sources show a pen name held as such beside the civil name (M.D. Coverley, Marjorie C. Luesebrink); in #940's terms that is a pseudonym kept and traceable to its bearer, and the sources show no distinct authorial function constituted under it. It holds a collaborative work under a collective's name and lists AI among its collections' qualities; what the sources show is preservation of authored works through migration, with authorship left with the author, and no record of how machine participation is attributed.",
